            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Create (Insert)</h2>
                    <p>Use <code>Add</code>/<code>AddRange</code> for tracked inserts and call <code>SaveChangesAsync</code> to persist; new entity keys are populated after saving.</p>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Single entity
var product = new Product { Name = "Laptop", Price = 999.99m };
context.Products.Add(product);
await context.SaveChangesAsync();
// product.Id is now set

// Multiple entities
var products = new List&lt;Product&gt;
{
    new() { Name = "Mouse", Price = 29.99m },
    new() { Name = "Keyboard", Price = 79.99m }
};
context.Products.AddRange(products);
await context.SaveChangesAsync();</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Read (Query)</h2>
                    <p>Use <code>FindAsync</code> for primary key lookups and LINQ methods for conditional queries; prefer async variants to avoid blocking threads.</p>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Get all
var allProducts = await context.Products.ToListAsync();

// Get by primary key (most efficient)
var product = await context.Products.FindAsync(id);

// Get single with condition
var laptop = await context.Products
    .FirstOrDefaultAsync(p =&gt; p.Name == "Laptop");

// Get single (throws if not exactly one)
var single = await context.Products
    .SingleOrDefaultAsync(p =&gt; p.Id == id);

// Check existence
var exists = await context.Products.AnyAsync(p =&gt; p.Id == id);</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Update</h2>
                    <p>Modify tracked entities directly and call <code>SaveChangesAsync</code>; for disconnected scenarios use <code>Update</code> or attach the entity and mark specific properties modified.</p>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Tracked entity (recommended)
var product = await context.Products.FindAsync(id);
if (product != null)
{
    product.Price = 899.99m;
    product.Name = "Gaming Laptop";
    await context.SaveChangesAsync();
}

// Disconnected entity
public async Task UpdateProductAsync(Product product)
{
    context.Products.Update(product);
    await context.SaveChangesAsync();
}

// Update specific properties only
context.Entry(product).Property(p =&gt; p.Price).IsModified = true;</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Delete</h2>
                    <p>Remove tracked entities or use bulk delete APIs (EF Core 7+) for efficient server-side deletions without loading entities.</p>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// With tracking
var product = await context.Products.FindAsync(id);
if (product != null)
{
    context.Products.Remove(product);
    await context.SaveChangesAsync();
}

// Without loading (EF Core 7+)
await context.Products
    .Where(p =&gt; p.Id == id)
    .ExecuteDeleteAsync();

// Bulk delete
await context.Products
    .Where(p =&gt; p.Price &lt; 10)
    .ExecuteDeleteAsync();</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Bulk Update (EF Core 7+)</h2>
                    <p>Use <code>ExecuteUpdateAsync</code> to perform server-side bulk updates efficiently without loading entities into memory.</p>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Update all products in category
await context.Products
    .Where(p =&gt; p.CategoryId == categoryId)
    .ExecuteUpdateAsync(setters =&gt; setters
        .SetProperty(p =&gt; p.Price, p =&gt; p.Price * 1.1m)
        .SetProperty(p =&gt; p.UpdatedAt, DateTime.UtcNow));</code></pre>
                </section>

                <LessonTakeaways>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Always call SaveChangesAsync() to persist changes.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>FindAsync is optimal for getting by primary key.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Use ExecuteUpdateAsync/ExecuteDeleteAsync for bulk operations.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Modify tracked entities directly, then save.</LessonTakeaway>
                </LessonTakeaways>
            </div>
